{% comment %}
Stage 3 of the decider — the kind follow-up (ruling 10). Stage 2 picked each step's coercion type by name; now, for a
step whose picked type carries kinds a program names, ask which kind: a number's int/long/double/decimal, an item's
json, a text's md/xml, a duration's iso/short/dotnet — or, for a generic (list, dict), its element type, the types
offered again. The answer combines with the picked type into {name, kind}. "none" keeps the type bare (`as text` with
no format names none). Only KindOf questions render here; a build with none renders {} and the stage is skipped.
The question keys and wording are pinned by PickListTests (PLang.Tests/Wire/App/Decider/pick_golden.json).
{% endcomment %}
{
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
{%- for s in goal.Step -%}
{%- assign text = s.Text -%}
{%- for q in s.Pick.Question -%}
{%- if q.Kind == "KindOf" -%}
{%- if q.Of == "list" or q.Of == "dict" -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. It coerces to a {{ q.Of }}. A {{ q.Of }} of what type — which type are its elements? Answer none if the step names no element type.{% endcapture -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ s.Index }} is `{{ text }}`. It coerces to `{{ q.Of }}`. Which kind of `{{ q.Of }}` does the step name? A word in the step beside the type word — one of the kinds offered here — names that kind; the type word and the kind word can sit together, in either order. None unless the step names one of these kinds; the type word alone (no kind word) names none.{% endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{ sep }}
  {{ q.Id | json }}: {
    "type": "choice",
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }},
    "criteria": {
{%- assign osep = "" -%}
{%- for v in q.Values -%}
{{ osep }}{{ v | json }}: null
{%- assign osep = ", " -%}
{%- endfor -%}
}
  }
{%- assign sep = "," -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor %}
}
